entityDescription:
The Common Wadden Sea Secretariat (CWSS) supports, facilitates and coordinates the Trilateral Wadden Sea Cooperation (TWSC). Located in Wilhelmshaven, the Secretariat was founded in 1987 by the Wadden Sea states Denmark, Germany, and the Netherlands.
The Secretariat
- coordinates, promotes and supports activities of the Cooperation;
- is responsible for the preparation and production of documents for ministerial conferences, meetings of the Wadden Sea Board (WSB) and trilateral work groups;
- collects and evaluates information on monitoring, protection and the ecological condition of the entire Wadden Sea;
- is the central contact for the UNESCO Wadden Sea World Heritage;
- produces and publishes reports by the Cooperation;
- involves the public in the protection of the entire Wadden Sea area through communications, awareness building and environmental education.
Since the inscription of the Wadden Sea on the UNESCO World Heritage List, the Secretariat moreover deals with the implementation of the obligations derived from the UNESCO World Heritage Convention.
The legal status and the functions of and regulations governing CWSS are stipulated in the Administrative Agreement concluded between the Danish, Dutch and German Ministries responsible for the Wadden Sea. Each Ministry finances a third of its budget. The working language of the Trilateral Cooperation and the CWSS is English.

Terradue Portugal, Unipessoal Lda is a Portuguese company active in the field of Earth Observation (EO), cloud-native processing platforms, and advanced geospatial data infrastructures.The company specialises in the design and validation of scalable EO cloud environments, supporting operational missions, downstream services, and emerging New Space operators requiring robust ground segment and data exploitation architectures.Terradue Portugal contributes to ESA and European programmes through:- system and cloud platform architecture design for EO ground segments and mission exploitation services;
- development and validation of processing workflows, Analysis Ready Data pipelines, and scalable data infrastructures;
- applied R&D in operational and near-operational contexts.
Terradue Portugal leverages expertise developed within the Terradue group, originally founded in 2006 as an ESA spin-off, applying this experience to next-generation EO data platforms and mission exploitation environments.

The University of Cassino and Southern Lazio (UNICAS) was established in 1979 as a response to the educational needs represented by an area characterized by a growing focus on innovation and cultural and social promotion. Due to its geographical location, UNICAS serves as a natural hub between the cities of southern Lazio, Campania, Molise and Abruzzo, from which it channels most of its students.
The University Community of the University consists of more than thirteen thousand people:
- 12,525 students enrolled in study courses and Postgraduate paths (a.y. 2021/2022);
- 275 faculty and researchers;
- 254 managers, technical and administrative staff;
- 9 staff and language experts;
- 122 PhD students;
- 42 research fellows.
Teaching and research activities take place mainly at the Cassino campus; 2 undergraduate and 2 master's degree courses in economics and engineering disciplines are hosted at the Frosinone decentralized pole, in order to contribute to the development of an increasingly fruitful interaction with the territory.
At the Gaeta campus, on the other hand, conference, public engagement and technology transfer activities are concentrated, as well as some continuing education activities.
The University provides paths for teaching qualification, structured according to current regulations. Services to students are provided through the 3 area libraries (economic-legal, engineering, humanities), the University Center for Orientation (CUOri), the University Center for Disability, Inclusion and Research (CUDIR), the Center for International Relations (CRI), The University Center for Information Services (CASI), and the Job Placement Office, at which an Information Desk is active, an interface between students, undergraduates and graduates with the world of work.
Teaching is supported by a lively and qualified research activity, developed within the Departments in all the fields of interest of the University (antiquistics, historical-artistic studies, historical, linguistic, philological-literary, paleographic-codicological, pedagogy and social service; mechanical, management, civil, environmental, electrical, computer, telecommunications engineering; economic, business and legal disciplines; motor and health sciences), with results of average high quality and peaks of national and international visibility and excellence. Research activities are supported by the presence of highly specialized laboratories, which are functional for the development of projects carried out also in the framework of national and international collaborations and for the release of technological consultancy for the benefit of institutions, entities and industries.
The research infrastructure and related equipment provided by the University is an important support for researchers' participation in competitive calls.

IETR is an academic research lab located in France (Rennes and Nantes).
Its main research areas and expertise domains span from material science for digital technologies to digital systems. They cover the following main disciplinary fields:

- Antennas & microwave devices over a very broad frequency spectrum extending from a few MHz to sub-THz;
- EMC and electromagnetism for biomedical;
- Multifunctional materials for miniaturization, reconfigurability, communications, sensing, energy recovery or storage;
- Microtechnologies and microsensors with various fabrication streams (low-temperature Silicon, organic electronics, biosourced electronics, etc.) for the study of circuits or microsensors;
- Digital communications systems and signal processing, as well as connected electronics and embedded systems;
- Remote sensing, multimodal imaging and propagation problems (indoor, outdoor, propagation in complex environments);
- Image analysis and processing (compression, prototyping, cryptography and content security, multimodal analysis, emotion analysis);
- Automatic (predictive control, adaptive control, energy management);
- Energy systems (transducers, conversion systems, energy networks, renewable energy smart grids, life cycle and eco-design of electrical systems).

IETR gathers about 400 members, half of them being yoing researchers (PhD students or post-doctoral fellows).

Most of IETR research projects are based on the demonstration of proofs of concepts made possible thanks to a large set of technical platforms and metrological / technological platforms, sometimes unique in the academic field on a national or European scale.
These experimental infrastructures, open to research collaborations (research projects, sub-contracting activities, etc.), deal with microwave metrology (from a few MHz to sub-THz), electronics and associated prototyping (M&sup2;ARS, QOSC and DIRAC platforms), airborne multimodal engineering (PIMA platform), HF radio technologies (ME-RISE platform), microtechnologies (NanoRennes platform, and CCMO for its training component) and multifunctional materials (MATRIX platform), electronic systems and on-board systems (Connected Objects platforms) image analysis and processing (DIVA platform and Hyperspectral Imaging platforms), hardware cybersecurity (Cyber-elec platform, Smart & secure room platform, energy systems and transducers (Exp&eacute;7 platform).

