The Lithuanian Non-Formal Education Agency (LINE&Scaron;A) (until 1 September 2023 &ndash; the Lithuanian Centre for Non-Formal Education of Students) is a budgetary institution subordinate to the Ministry of Education, Science and Sports, providing assistance in the implementation of state policy in the areas of non-formal education of children and vocational guidance (career education).
LINE&Scaron;A tasks:
- to develop the system of non-formal education for children;
- to organize, within its competence, information and qualification improvement of participants in the education system;
- to coordinate and carry out vocational guidance for students;
- to create and develop a STEAM education ecosystem;
- to create conditions for the talents and creativity of highly motivated students to unfold and to ensure students' participation in international events.

Galgo Management Systems offers consultancy services to public and private organisations with a view to:
1) simplifying the complexity of their Management System;
2) obtaining Quality certifications such as the ISO 9001:2026 standard;
3) facilitating changes within the organisation.
These services involve reviewing and optimising all working methods, processes, procedures, guidelines and support tools by eliminating duplications, gaps, inaccuracies and ambiguities, in order to make the Management System as streamlined and efficient as possible.
We also support change management using facilitation tools such as conflict management, coaching and mediation in multicultural environments.

Forestry France is the leading independent forestry expertise and management company in France. For over 100 years, the company has supported public and private landowners in valuing and preserving their natural heritage. Forestry France supports the resilience of territories through the sustainable management of forests, tree heritage, agricultural land and infrastructure.
Its activity is organized around 6 complementary business units, reflecting the breadth of its expertise: 
- For&ecirc;t (Forests), its historic core business, dedicated to the management and enhancement of forest estates; 
- Arbre (Trees, urban trees), focused on the management of tree heritage, particularly in urban and peri-urban settings; 
- Infra-r&eacute;seaux (Infrastructure, major networks), which manages vegetation along linear infrastructure (roads, railways, networks) and oversees solar farm projects; 
- Agri (Agriculture, agronomy), covering rural leases, land expertise, and agroforestry; 
- Bureau d'&Eacute;tudes (Studies), providing cross-cutting technical and scientific support; 
- Training center (Qualiopi-certified), which shares this expertise with industry professionals.
This structure allows Forestry France to address the full range of challenges related to natural heritage management, well beyond forestry alone. Internationally, the group operates primarily across Europe through its involvement in Forestry Europe, while remaining open to opportunistic engagements elsewhere.

N.P.C. New Production Concept S.r.l. Is a dynamic company operating in the mechatronics, packaging and aerospace sectors with leading activities in the assembly and integration of complex automatic machines. 
Since 2013 through the SPACEMIND business unit, the company has been engaged in research and development activities aimed at the commercialization of integrated solutions in the Space and Ground Segment for civil and defense applications. The company's strength behind the business idea is to offer qualified aerospace engineering know-how, combined with more than 20 years of experience in managing complex automated systems. N.P.C. is participated by CURTI Spa and ECOR Spa: the former is a leading mechanical and automation manufacturing company with consolidated experience and capabilities in manufacturing for the aerospace sector. ECOR is a company specializing in the supply of stainless steel and special alloy products with capabilities in mechanical manufacturing and machining and rapid prototyping in metal sintering in the defense and aerospace sectors.
Today N.P.C. can count on 70 employees with more than 6,000 m2 of space for design, assembly, testing and warehousing. The production process has always been characterized from the beginning by a strong focus on the quality management system, which today has led to the certification ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 14100.
SPACEMIND has proven experience in the design, manufacture, and integration of CubeSats platforms, focusing on flexibility and short lead times while ensuring the highest levels of quality, offering:
End-to-end missions: from requirements to on-orbit operations, with a lean, customer-focused approach;
Complete platforms from 1U to 16U, customized to payload requirements;
High-performance separation systems (Deployers) for CubSats;
Cubesat hardware: a portfolio of subsystems based on experience in various Cubesat missions;
High-speed and high-precision ground tracking solutions (SSA and SST applications) and on-orbit object tracking

