description:
Specializing in advanced technologies, Voyager Technologies Europe manages scientific experiments aboard the International Space Station (ISS), with over 2,000 payloads flown to date, and develops critical infrastructure for government, commercial, and scientific missions, ranging from low Earth orbit to space exploration. The company operates under a Space Act Agreement with NASA, a partnership framework that enables collaborative research and technology development on the ISS. Voyager Technologies Europe, based in Turin, provides hosting of scientific experiments aboard the International Space Station (ISS), offering a unique environment for autonomous testing or direct astronaut-assisted, alongside satellite deployment services in low Earth orbit (LEO). Specifically, the company offers: 
•	Payload designing support •	Launch and access to the ISS; 
•	The utilization of proprietary facilities aboard the ISS; 
•	Payload design and development; 
•	Manifesting and safety review; 
•	Clean room and testing; 
•	In-orbit payload operations; 
•	Payload returns from the ISS. 
A comprehensive approach that combines cutting-edge research and operational solutions for government, commercial, and scientific space missions.

entityDescription:
Estellus-MW is an SME located in Coueron (France). It has been recently created and it originates from Estellus (Paris, France), created in 2009. Estellus-MW is an engineering company specialised in the processing and exploitation of microwave satellite data for earth observations. The services developed by the company are based on the expertise of their employees, who are international experts in their fields.
Estellus-MW provides services in the following areas:
&bull; The development of radiative transfer modeling algorithms and inversion methods for the processing of satellite microwave observations;
&bull; The production of geophysical data from satellite observations, particularly those obtained from microwave instruments;
&bull; The creation, evaluation, and interpretation of time series of geophysical products derived from satellite observations, for environmental and climate studies;
&bull; The contribution to the design of new earth observation instruments in the field of microwave radiometry;
&bull; The preparation of microwave instrument simulators in order to assess the performance of newspace missions and prepare for the exploitation of their data.

The ITA is a public, non-profit research technological center attached to the Department of Presidency, Economy, and Justice of the Government of Aragon. Its mission is to contribute to the technological development of companies and increase their competitiveness.
ITA carries out R&D&I projects, providing multidisciplinary technological knowledge through a team of more than 280 highly qualified technologists. This team's scientific and technical excellence is oriented toward solving your business needs in a personalized way, with the aim of making your company more competitive and excellent through innovation and technological development.
The core values of support, collaboration (linkage), and technology transfer reinforce the partnership with companies in R&D&I projects. Companies consider us as their own innovation and R&D teams, relying on us to provide cutting-edge technologies aimed at adding value in the design of new products, the improvement and optimization of processes, and support in the creation of new disruptive business models.
ITA has defined five strategic areas of action to respond to the challenges of society, always offering their technological know-how:
Safe, sustainable, and connected mobility;
A digital agribusiness that responds to the demand for healthier and safer food;
An efficient industry that is fully digitized and focused on the circular economy;
Smart health that improves people&rsquo;s lives;
Clean energy that favors efficiency and the use of renewable energies.
These areas are interconnected due to global societal demands, and by addressing them together, ITA aims to create a more digital, green, and social world.

Open Impact is an accredited spin-off of the University of Milano-Bicocca that provides services and develops digital products for measuring, enhancing and managing of impacts through an integrated sustainability approach. Open Impact was founded in 2019 thanks to the meeting of a mix of experiences and skills coming from the world of academic research, social innovation and digital development. By collecting and systematising a huge amount of internationally validated open- source impact assessments, Open Impact has managed to create the first database in Italy for im&shy; pact benchmarking. The Open Impact Database is designed to support organisations in identifying the impacts they generate, linking them to the 17 UN SGDs and other sustaina&shy; bility taxonomies, such as BES and ESG.

Services:
&middot; pact Strategy - We accompany organizations to recognize impact as a strategic asset and to build more desirable futures around it;
&middot; Impact Management - Through our digital platform we support organizations in ma&shy; naging the impact cycle of their initiatives, from the forecasting phases to the visualiza&shy; tion of their impact evidence;

&middot; Impact Research - Research is what we put as the starting and ending point of each of our processes;

&middot; Impact Investing - We support the construction of impact-oriented ecosystems and projects, promoting multistakeholder interaction to respond to complex social challen&shy; ges.

Products:

&middot; Impact measurement & management - We have developed digital tools that support impactmanagement, from the predictive phase to the automatic measurement and vi&shy; sualisation of data. The tools comply with the Impact Management standards.
&middot; Sustainability assessment & reporting - We have developed digital tools for reporting and assessing the sustainability of organisations.

Nova Reply (Business Unit of NET Reply SPA) is the Reply Group company whose mission is to guide its Customers in the Digital Transformation process for the adoption of next-generation networks, which will allow pervasively distributed connectivity.
The goal is to focus on the Aerospace and Defense markets, through a set of services which highlight on the following three offer segments:
1. Development of "Ubiquitous Networks", on terrestrial, space/satellite and submarine domains for the development of integrated connectivity solutions;
2. Creation of platforms and solutions for the orchestration of ubiquitous networks, for Network-as-a-Service applications;
3. Vertical applications: use cases and design, development and automation of services.

Sustain Orbit is an early stage start up with a mission to enable the sustainable and prosperous space economy that humanity needs. We believe that space sustainability and prosperity are two sides of the same coin. 

Our research and development is focused on:
- Mitigating and minimising space debris;
- Utilising engineered timber for its low environmental impact and advantageous engineering qualities;
- Designing for manufacturability, modularity, and scale. 

We believe that wood opens the door to a whole new discipline of space engineering, where existing constraints are redrawn. One example of many is that wood is RF transparent, as opposed to metal. What new opportunities emerge when RF engineering and integration isn't a battle against the very fabric of the spacecraft?

Seatrackbox d&eacute;veloppe une solution technologique innovante r&eacute;pondant aux enjeux majeurs de la s&eacute;curit&eacute; maritime et de la protection des &eacute;cosyst&egrave;mes marins. Notre dispositif permet de localiser et de suivre les containers tomb&eacute;s en mer gr&acirc;ce &agrave; des capteurs intelligents et &agrave; une analyse en temps r&eacute;el des donn&eacute;es collect&eacute;es.
Cette approche proactive contribue &agrave; :
- Pr&eacute;venir les risques en mer, en d&eacute;tectant rapidement les chutes de containers et en facilitant les interventions d&rsquo;urgence ;
- Limiter les pertes logistiques et renforcer la s&eacute;curit&eacute; des routes maritimes ;
- R&eacute;duire l&rsquo;impact environnemental, en identifiant les incidents polluants et en fournissant des donn&eacute;es pr&eacute;cises sur les sources de contamination ;
- Soutenir la pr&eacute;servation de la biodiversit&eacute; marine, en agissant concr&egrave;tement contre la pollution oc&eacute;anique.
&Agrave; l&rsquo;intersection de la technologie de pointe et de l&rsquo;engagement environnemental, Seatrackbox se positionne comme un acteur cl&eacute; de la transition vers une &eacute;conomie bleue durable, en apportant des solutions concr&egrave;tes et mesurables aux d&eacute;fis maritimes contemporains.

