AREU is the regional public emergency healthcare system in the Lombardy region in Italy. It&rsquo;s an agency with the goal of standardizing responses and performance, and it is closely integrated with the healthcare and social healthcare facilities throughout the region to ensure continuity of care for citizens. AREU&rsquo;s work extends across the entire regional serving a population of approximately 10 million inhabitants.In accordance with our regional guidelines, AREU guarantees the following services across the region:
&middot; Intra-regional and inter-regional coordination, direction, management, implementation, and monitoring of the pre-hospital Emergency Urgency System (Service 118);
&middot; Operation of the Single Emergency Number (NUE) 112;
&middot; Operation of the European Harmonized Number 116117 (NEA), providing non-urgent medical care with a social;
&middot; Logistical coordination for the collection, transport, and transplantation of organs and tissues;
&middot; Coordination of transfusion activities, blood exchange flows, and compensation of blood, blood components, and blood products.
Also, AREU collaborates with the Civil Protection system to handle major emergencies and promotes scientific research activities. We offer specific training and refresher courses for professionals involved in the Agency&rsquo;s activities.

Spin Life guides public and private companies in analyzing and implementing strategic and sustainable solutions. It helps organizations and local communities in reinventing themselves, optimizing their processes and certifying their progresses, creating a bridge between business and sustainability.
Its science based approach is the fundamental pillar of all the activities we perform. It is based on 4 steps:

- CONTEXT ANALYSIS. It analyses the operations and the entire life cycle starting from one or more products. We analyse the market and the stakeholders to define the factors that can jeopardize the competitiveness of an organisation;
- ANALYSIS OF THE ENVIRONMENTAL PERFORMANCES OF A PRODUCT OR PROCESS. Quantification of the environmental performances via an assessment of all the potential environmental impacts according to the Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) methodology;
- OPTIMISATION AND IMPROVEMENT.
It provides solutions to reduce resource consumption and environmental impacts. It develops management and optimisation practices to guide the decision-makingprocess;
- CERTIFICATION ANDCOMMUNICATION. It support organisations in certifying their products with low environmental impact. It identifies corporate environmental and social responsibility projects that can enhance the image and reputation of a company.

GROW UP is a social agricultural enterprise based in Turin and Pinerolo, established to promote an innovative and replicable model of urban and peri-urban agriculture, blending rural tradition with advanced technologies. As a Third Sector Entity, it integrates sustainable food production, environmental education, social inclusion, and urban regeneration.
It operates through two key locations: Cascina Cassotti Balbo (the first officially recognized Educational Farm in the City of Turin) and Cascina Ainana in Pinerolo, where it develops resilient agricultural practices such as aquaponics, composting, regenerative agriculture, and alpaca farming (Alpaca del Monviso project).
Its activities include:
Accredited Educational Farm for schools, families, and vocational training;

Social Farm and Animal-Assisted Interventions (AAI);

Work inclusion projects for people in vulnerable conditions;

Environmental education and urban climate action projects;

Development of energy communities and local food supply chains.

GROW UP adheres to the Disability Agenda, promotes the One Health approach, and participates in local and European networks in the fields of agroecology, social innovation, and environmental sustainability.

