Irreo is an irrigation automation system with crop monitoring by satellite.
Irreo is a system that allows automatic and efficient management of irrigation on all sectors of a cultivated plot of land, combining an irrigation automation system and a satellite monitoring service for crops and their water requirements without the installation of probes or sensors.
Our algorithms analyse maps from various satellite constellations, both public and private, on a daily basis to estimate the actual evapotranspiration of the crops and provide water to the plants in the right amount and at the right time interval to meet their water needs.
To this end, we have designed and developed electronic control units that, connected to the irrigation system, autonomously manage the flow of water, respecting the constraints and programmes imposed by the farmer, so as to calibrate the irrigation process according to the water needs of each sector of the field.
With Irreo, users can:
- monitor the health, growth and water requirements of crops in the various plots;
- receive an optimal and realistic irrigation schedule for the crops on its field, taking into account the water requirements of the plants on the various sectors, the constraints of the irrigation system, and the user's preferences in terms of rotations and strategies;
- automatically start irrigation, distributing the right amount of water at the right time interval, leaving the user the possibility of managing the system remotely (motor pump, filters, solenoid valves...) through our simple app and thus being able to increase crop yields while reducing working hours, costs and consumption.
With Irreo, the farm can:
- Increase crop yields: produce more with the same amount of water used, also improving the quality of the harvest and reducing the risk of damage or loss;
- increase the work productivity of its employees;
- optimise water use, thereby reducing the energy costs associated with irrigation activities;
- keep crop health under control;
- remotely manage the irrigation system and monitor its proper functioning;
- save on the purchase and maintenance costs of soil moisture sensors.

Ukatemi Technologies is a focused, professional engineering company with expertise and demonstrated experience providing high quality and unique cybersecurity services to its Customers. We approach problems with an engineering attitude. We enjoy dissecting things to understand them better, we are excited by designing new solutions, we care about small details in implementation, and we always strive for quality. Our motto is&bdquo;Driven by challenges&rdquo;,that means we aim to apply our expertise in protecting applications, systems and services that require high quality of service, reliability and security, and in specific areas where there are no well-developed solutions yet.

Ukatemi was founded in 2012 as a spin-off company of the renowned CrySyS Lab (Laboratory of Cryptography and System Security) of the Budapest University of Technology and Economics. Ukatemi is an independent SME based in Budapest, Hungary.

Our capabilities include evaluating cybersecurity posture, penetration testing and vulnerability assessment, reverse engineering, security by design (systems and processes), incident response, computer forensics, malware analysis, fine-tuning SIEM/SOC solutions as well as designing and performing practice-oriented cybersecurity training and exercises both in IT and OT (ICS/SCADA) environment. We have strong experience in the field of malware analysis and cyber-physical systems security.

Each Ukatemi engineer is an established and skilled professional. Our staff has been involved in the detection and analysis of several publicized targeted malware attacks (including Duqu, Flame, MiniDuke, TeamSpy), custom-tested anti-APT tools, played key roles in large-scale incident management, security and vulnerability assessment and security evaluation of critical information infrastructures; we have provided support to many IT security experts worldwide. Our team of qualified experts has the professional skills and experience needed to deliver the high quality and efficient performance of the activities described in this proposal.

We have:

&middot;deep and robust knowledge in malware analysis, de-obfuscation techniques, and reverse-engineering;
&middot;widespread experience in cyber-physical systems, especially in industrial control systems (including oil and gas; electricity and nuclear power; utility; production; IoT; automotive and transportation);
&middot;access to private malware and threat intelligence feeds and repositories, as well as our own malware repository with more than 600 million malware samples and a collection of 10 million public key certificates;
&middot;custom sandbox environments and malware laboratory, including custom tools;
&middot;experience with various cyber threats including targeted attacks (APTs);
&middot;top level NATO, EU and national security clearance certificate, professional liability insurance, and we operate an ISO qualified quality (9001) and information security (27001) management system;
&middot;20 engineering experts (4 with Ph.D, 11 with MsC, 5 with BsC degree) with OSCP, CREST CPSA, CREST CRT, GIAC GPEN, CEH, CISSP,ISO 27001 LA certifications among others.

UNEP/GRID-Warsaw Centre was established on 17 September 1991 pursuant to the official agreement signed between the Director of the United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP) and the Polish Government (Ministry of the Environment, Forestry, and Natural Resources), as a centre working within the Global Resource Information Database (GRID) network. Formally, the Centre has been established in the structures of the National Foundation for Environmental Protection (hence, it has the non-profit status).
The Centre actively co-operates with self-government authorities, educational institutions and private companies pursuing corporate social responsibility (CSR) principles in a wide range of projects devoted to effective environmental management, application of remote sensing, geographic information systems (GIS), and environmental education.
Specific areas of expertise and activity of the UNEP/GRID-Warsaw Centre entail the following:
&middot; geoinformation and remote sensing: analyses of spatial data on environmental and socio-economic phenomena and processes; geodatabase development and maintenance (incl. data harmonisation according to the INSPIRE implementing rules); development and market application of GIS solutions and geoportals; practical implementation of result of scientific discovery related to novel geoinformation tools and methods;
&middot; environmental governance and reporting: thematic mapping and geovisualisation, incl. 3D modelling; development of GIS and ICT applications to support decision making and spatial planning by public administration units; use of mobile GIS-based tools and techniques to support monitoring and rapid mapping activities; implementation of the INSPIRE Directive in Poland;
&middot; capacity building: specialized trainings, workshops, seminars, conferences; e-Learning courses; educational materials and publications &ndash; targeted primarily at public administration bodies and related to the use of remote sensing tools, GIS tools and applications (with focus on open source solutions), spatial data for environmental management, spatial planning, crisis management, etc.
&middot; environmental campaigns, environmental education, public participation: using modern multimedia and other ICT solutions; youth education and awareness building on issues related to environment/nature protection, community involvement, building ICT literacy; fostering public and inter-institutional consultations, e.g. in spatial planning procedures, aided by geoinformation tools and methods (geo-consultations); citizen science; CSR and sustainable business practices;

The ENTENTE pour la for&ecirc;t m&eacute;diterran&eacute;enne, known as ENTENTE VALABRE, is an independent public administrative body that works closely with the Ministries of the Interior, Ecological Transition and Territorial Cohesion (MTECT) and Agriculture. As a key interdepartmental player at both institutional and territorial level, VALABRE's main challenge is to protect people and areas from major natural hazards.
Bringing together 31 local authorities, including 15 d&eacute;partements, 15 Services D&eacute;partementaux d'Incendie et de Secours (SDIS) and the Collectivit&eacute; Territoriale de Corse, its missions focus on the pooling of skills and resources, as well as consultation with its partners, with the aim of optimising the management of major risks. The organisation is divided into 4 departments:
- The Information and Prevention of Major Risks Department ;
- The Civil Security Training School (ECASC);
- The Test and Research Centre (CEREN);
- The Innovation and New Technologies Centre (PONT).

The PONT offers its members a suite of technological solutions covering all the needs associated with managing forest fires and fires in natural areas, from prevention to operational response, feedback and continuous improvement. VALABRE is strategically positioned as a provider of shared operational solutions, with a coherent vision at territorial level. The COP CRIMSON, used by the Centre Op&eacute;rationnel de Gestion Interminist&eacute;rielle des Crises (COGIC), the 7 Centres Op&eacute;rationnels de Zone de d&eacute;fense (COZ) and more than 50 fired departments, continues to be deployed in France (SDIS, departmental councils, local authorities) and internationally. The CRIMSON tool also provides real-time information to the ORSEC and SYNAPSE national crisis management platforms, making VALABRE the only French entity authorised to supply these Ministry of the Interior networks. Once operational, the NEXIS project, which aims to pool the Alert Management Systems (SGA) and Operational Management Systems (SGO) used in the SDIS, will also incorporate a CRIMSON gateway.
The PONT also keeps a proactive watch on innovative technologies, with the aim of enhancing its services to end users (emergency services, civil protection, inter-municipalities, regional authorities, etc.). For example, PONT was commissioned by MTECT to carry out the PANOPT&Egrave;S study, the aim of which is to deploy a system for the early detection (<5 minutes) of all forest fires and fires in natural areas on a national (metropolitan) scale, and to monitor them in near-real time (burnt areas, fire fronts, fire breaks, hot spots, etc.). This early detection is in line with the national operational doctrine of "massive attack on incipient fires".

Founded in 1948 as an agricultural college, today Hartpury University and Hartpury College is a thriving community with over 690 members of staff supporting over 4,500 students. The 360-hectare rural campus in the heart of Gloucestershire is home to extensive facilities and resources that enrich the lives of students, staff, local and regional communities and the wider world. 

Hartpury is a unique and specialist education provider offering courses from diploma-level through to postgraduate degree-level in the specialisms of Animal, Agriculture, Equine, Sport, and Veterinary Nursing. Our unrelenting commitment to educational excellence has seen us nurture talent and produce well-rounded graduates across all our specialisms, backed up by the latest Graduate Outcomes 2023 data that shows 97% of former students are now in employment, further study or engaged with another purposeful activity. Most recently, Hartpury University has been awarded Gold in all three areas of the Teaching Excellence Framework (TEF) - Overall, Student Experience, and Student Outcomes. This impressive accolade places Hartpury in the top 15% of published UK-wide institutions. Hartpury is also the only Gloucestershire university to have been awarded the prestigious triple Gold status.

Hartpury has many outstanding assets to support teaching, research and knowledge exchange, including: 
